@scene chapter_6b_loom_of_words

background: night_valley.avif
music: wisdom_theme.mp3

dialogue:
"West, the land turns strange and soft. Threads of light hang in the air, each strung with tiny glowing runes."
"At the centre of the web a woman works an enormous loom, weaving threads into sentences and unpicking them again."

background: riddle_weaver

npc Riddle Weaver:
"A traveller of letters, letter by letter, arrives —"
"— though not yet lettered enough to read the letters, I'd wager."

npc You:
"...I didn't understand a single word of that."

npc Riddle Weaver:
"No. Not yet. But you will — thread by thread."
"Sit. Words are the last thread before functions, and the finest. Learn the whole weave."

system skill_learned:
"MODULE UNLOCKED"
"THE LOOM OF WORDS"
"index · slice · upper/lower · split/join · f-strings · immutability"

dialogue:
"— LESSON I — THE RIBBON —"
"She lays a shining word across the loom, each rune a separate bead of light."

npc Riddle Weaver:
"A word is a ribbon of runes, numbered from zero — the same counting the Quartermaster drilled into you."
"Take one rune by its number. Or take a whole run of them with a slice, stopping — as ever — one short of the end."

interactive: loom_slice

dialogue:
"— LESSON II — RESHAPE THE THREAD —"
"She runs a finger down the ribbon; the runes flare bright, then dim."

npc Riddle Weaver:
"A thread can be RAISED to capitals, or LOWERED to whispers. It can be TRIMMED of the empty space at its ends."
"upper. lower. strip. Small spells, but they save a riddle from being misread."

interactive: loom_methods

dialogue:
"— LESSON III — CUT AND GATHER —"
"She snips a ribbon into pieces, then gathers the pieces onto a single new thread."

npc Riddle Weaver:
"split cuts a ribbon wherever you say, and leaves you a LIST of pieces."
"join is its mirror — it gathers a list of pieces back onto one ribbon, with a thread of your choosing between them."

interactive: loom_split_join

dialogue:
"— LESSON IV — THE TRUE WEAVE —"
"Now she smiles, and the whole loom leans in."

npc Riddle Weaver:
"And here is the art I am known for. Do not merely SHOW a value beside your words — WEAVE it in."
"Mark the ribbon with an f, and any name in braces is replaced by its value, right where it sits."
"Build me one. A name and a rank, woven into a single line."

interactive: loom_fstring_forge

dialogue:
"— LESSON V — THE THREAD REMEMBERS —"
"She tries to recut a finished ribbon; it will not take the blade."

npc Riddle Weaver:
"One last truth, easily missed. A ribbon, once woven, cannot be UNPICKED in place."
"Raise it, trim it, add to it — each spell spins a NEW thread and leaves the old one exactly as it was."
"A string never changes. It is only ever replaced."

interactive: loom_immutable

npc Riddle Weaver:
"So — thread, or bundle? Tell me at a glance what each spell leaves in your hand."

interactive: loom_sort

dialogue:
"— PROVE IT — SAY IT LOUDER —"
"She hands you a word so softly spun you can barely hear it."

npc Riddle Weaver:
"This one must open a door, and it hasn't the voice. Raise it to a shout — all capitals, an edge on the end."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Store in shouted the word in all capitals with a single '!' added to the end."

mission: loom_shout

background: riddle_weaver

npc Riddle Weaver:
"Louder. Better. Now the weave itself — the thing the gate ahead demands."

dialogue:
"— COMBINE IT — WEAVE A TITLE —"
"She gestures up the mountain, to the sealed gate at the tower's foot."

npc Riddle Weaver:
"That gate answers only to a traveller named PROPERLY. Take the first name from a full one, and weave it into a title fit for a door."
"Practise it here, on my loom, where a wrong thread costs nothing. Cut, take, and weave — all three at once."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Take the first word of full_name and weave into title_card: <first> the <rank>."

mission: loom_titlecard

background: night_valley.avif

dialogue:
"You cut the first name loose, weave it into a title, and speak it into the threads."
"The loom holds the words a moment, approves of them, and lets them go."

background: night_forest.avif

npc Riddle Weaver:
"There. Cut, gathered, and woven true."
"But a thread you cannot draw twice was never yours. Draw it once more, cold."

interactive: loom_final_recall

npc Riddle Weaver:
"Split, taken, raised. The whole loom, in your hands now."
"Then come. There is a gate on the way up that will not open for an apprentice."

dialogue:
"She rises from the loom for the first time, and the threads part to let you both through."

system level_up:
"CHAPTER COMPLETE"
"The Loom of Words"
"Mastered: slicing · upper/lower · split/join · f-strings · immutability"

reward:
xp: 75
gold: 45
achievement: NAMED AND WOVEN

next:
chapter_6_riddle_weaver
